{
  "info": {
    "name": "MCQ Online Test Platform API",
    "description": "Role-based REST API for the MCQ Online Test Platform: examiners manage a\nquestion bank and review results, while examinees take a 50-question\nmultiple-choice test.\n\n## Roles\n\n| Role | How authenticated | Capabilities |\n|------|-------------------|--------------|\n| **Examinee** | `POST /auth/examinee/entry` (PRN + name) | Take the test, review answers, export own data |\n| **Examiner** | `POST /auth/examiner/login` (username + password) | Manage questions, view session results, read settings |\n| **Admin examiner** | Examiner login with admin flag | Additionally create examiners, update settings, request GDPR erasure |\n\n## Authentication\n\nAuthentication uses an **opaque server-side session** stored in Redis and\ndelivered via an HttpOnly `session_id` cookie (path `/api/v1`,\n`SameSite=strict`). There are no bearer tokens. Cookies are set by the login\nand entry endpoints and cleared by `POST /auth/logout`.\n\n## CSRF protection\n\nAll mutating endpoints (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) on authenticated routes\nrequire the `X-CSRF-Token` header. The session-bound token is returned by\n`GET /auth/me`; a pre-login token for the login forms is available from\n`GET /auth/csrf`.\n\n## Response conventions\n\n- **Success** responses wrap the payload in an envelope:\n  `{ \"data\": ..., \"meta\": { \"request_id\": \"...\" } }`.\n- **Errors** are returned as RFC 7807 problem details with content type\n  `application/problem+json` (see the `ProblemDetails` schema). Validation\n  failures return **400** with a field-level `errors` array.\n- Every response carries an `X-Request-Id` header that matches\n  `meta.request_id`, for log correlation.\n- File downloads (data export, CSV export) bypass the envelope and return\n  raw content with a `Content-Disposition: attachment` header.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "expectedStatus",
      "value": "200"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Issue a pre-login CSRF token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf",
            "description": "Issue a standalone CSRF token for pre-authentication flows.\n\nUse the returned token in the `X-CSRF-Token` header when calling the login\nand entry endpoints from a browser form. After authentication, prefer the\nsession-bound token returned by `GET /auth/me`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"expectedStatus\", \"200\");"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const ok = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"expectedStatus\").split(\",\").map(s => parseInt(s.trim(), 10));",
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is expected\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(ok).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Response time under 5s\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
